# Verdict

**NOT CONVERGED.** Five blocking contract defects reproduced independently, plus two non-blocking documentation/tooling findings.

The worktree was not modified. `git status --short` remains:

```text
?? docs/scratch/arrival-break/sol-s4-integration-r1-stdout.log
```

All custom probes were written under `/tmp/sol-s4-r1/`.

## Findings

### finding/s4-sol-r1-gf3-multiclass-loss — BLOCKING

File: [legacy_source.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/migrate/src/migrate/legacy_source.py:271), especially lines 271–341; contradictory test at [test_inventory.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/migrate/tests/test_inventory.py:201).

A batch containing `alice`, `bob`, and `observer=""` is recorded only under `mixed_observer_lines`. The absent/empty class is omitted, and the empty spelling becomes the misleading phrase “missing observer.” This violates enumeration across every applicable class and spelling-distinct empty-observer census.

Probe:

```text
$ .venv/bin/python /tmp/sol-s4-r1/probe_gf3_multiclass.py
codec_invalid_lines=()
mixed_observer_lines=((1, ('alice', 'bob'), 1),)
absent_observer_lines=()
target_exists=False
FAIL: the offending line was not enumerated in every applicable class
```

The current test explicitly locks the incorrect behavior with `len(exc.absent_observer_lines) == 0`.

### finding/s4-sol-r1-resume-incomplete-draft-diff — BLOCKING

File: [sidecar.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/migrate/src/migrate/sidecar.py:841), lines 841–873.

Resume compares `kind`, `observer`, `origin`, and `body`, but omits `RecordDraft.authored_at` and `RecordDraft.signature`. Full verification and logical-row equivalence do not close this gap. Consequently, resume can publish a target that is not byte-identical to the re-derived draft stream and can contain outer-signed migrated records.

Outer-signature probe:

```text
expected_draft_signature=None
resumed_target_signature='A3g3up5XEFsVU2w9hD4VJMSq3StMoIy4o6jmayI7Hzyf1ck/...'
migration_published=True
target_bytes_unchanged=True
FAIL: resume accepted and published an outer-signed migrated record
```

Authored-time probe:

```text
expected_authored_at=1.0
resumed_target_authored_at=1000.0
target_bytes_unchanged=True
FAIL: resume accepted and published a non-byte-identical draft timestamp
```

### finding/s4-sol-r1-resume-breaks-lineage-naming — BLOCKING

File: [sidecar.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/migrate/src/migrate/sidecar.py:756), lines 756–783.

Fresh targets are lineage-named, but `resume_target` accepts and publishes any filename without checking `<lineage>.arrival`.

```text
lineage=01M1AZM7JCQK36D4FMERSKWBTK
target_name=friendly-name.arrival
required_name=01M1AZM7JCQK36D4FMERSKWBTK.arrival
FAIL: resume published a non-lineage-named staging target
```

No rename occurred; the descriptor was published against the friendly filename.

### finding/s4-sol-r1-custodian-authority-source — BLOCKING

Files:

- [transform.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/migrate/src/migrate/transform.py:195), lines 195–221
- [sidecar.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/migrate/src/migrate/sidecar.py:638), lines 638–713
- [store.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/apps/loops/src/loops/commands/store.py:830), lines 830–854
- [signing.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/custody/src/custody/signing.py:104), lines 104–141

There are two manifestations of one authority-source error:

1. Custody defines the self-observer as `vertex_path.stem`, and the CLI probes that identity. `transform()` instead defaults to `VertexFile.name`. Valid vertices whose declared name differs from their filename fail migration.

```text
vertex_stem='project'
vertex_declared_name='display-name'
exit_code=2
stderr=✗ project: Custodian 'display-name' has no public key declared in .vertex observers block
FAIL: CLI passed VertexFile.name as custodian and refused a keyed self-observer
```

2. Public `custodian`/`custodian_key` overrides allow a direct caller to bypass the declaration entirely.

```text
declared_vertex_name='alice'
genesis_observer='mallory'
genesis_key_is_declared_alice=False
FAIL: public overrides bypassed the declared custodian identity and key
```

This contradicts the ruling that the custodian is the vertex self-observer and genesis is checked against the declaration’s identity and key.

### finding/s4-sol-r1-surgical-publish-deletes-comments — BLOCKING

Files:

- [loader.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/lang/src/lang/loader.py:974), lines 974–1089
- [ast.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/lang/src/lang/ast.py:698), lines 698–708
- [sidecar.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/migrate/src/migrate/sidecar.py:204), lines 204–315

`effective_store_clause()` deliberately returns the entire physical line. Replacing that span deletes same-line comments and other non-store text. AST re-parse equality cannot detect comment loss.

```text
edited_store_line=store "./target.arrival" backend="file"
marker_preserved=False
FAIL: surgical publish deleted a same-line operator comment
```

That is not a surgical store-clause edit preserving every other byte.

### finding/s4-sol-r1-doc-truth-drift — non-blocking

Files:

- [CLAUDE.md](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/migrate/CLAUDE.md:55), lines 55–61
- [sidecar.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/migrate/src/migrate/sidecar.py:50), lines 50–57 and 968–975
- ignored [ARCHITECTURE.md](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/docs/dev/ARCHITECTURE.md:57), lines 57–69 and 142–149

Current false claims include:

- Stage 2 calls the randomly minted lineage “deterministic.”
