## Findings

### finding/s4-sol-r2-hash-raw-store-span — BLOCKING

Files:

- [loader.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/lang/src/lang/loader.py:974), especially lines 1011–1061
- [sidecar.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/migrate/src/migrate/sidecar.py:209)

The new `_scan_kdl_node_end()` recognizes hash-raw strings only when `r#"... "#` starts a token. For an embedded property such as:

```kdl
store "./legacy.jsonl" backend=r#"fi" fake"# // KEEP OPERATOR " tail
```

the bare-property branch treats the raw string’s embedded quote as an ordinary closing quote. It then consumes through the quote in the trailing comment. The returned span includes the comment; verification-by-reparse cannot detect comment loss, so publish succeeds and deletes it.

The grammar deliberately admits any non-empty backend name for adapters supplied by other deployments, so this is a valid parsed descriptor shape; it is not malformed-input handling ([ast.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/lang/src/lang/ast.py:688)).

Probe:

```text
$ uv run python /tmp/sol-s4-r2/probe_scanner_raw.py
hash_raw_property: count=1 span=(15, 52) slice='store "./legacy.jsonl" backend=r#"fi"'
hash_raw_property: edit=ACCEPTED
hash_raw_property: edited_line='store "./target.arrival" backend="file" // OLD PROPERTY BYTES"# // KEEP COMMENT' old_property_bytes_leaked=True
hash_raw_deletes_comment: count=1 span=(15, 83) slice='store "./legacy.jsonl" backend=r#"fi" fake"# // KEEP OPERATOR " tail'
hash_raw_deletes_comment: edit=ACCEPTED
hash_raw_deletes_comment: edited_line='store "./target.arrival" backend="file"' marker_preserved=False
FAIL: accepted hash-raw rewrites used an incorrect clause span
probe_scanner_raw_rc=1
```

The same probe includes two bounded cases that refuse without writing; those satisfy the stated “refuse-shaped or correct” criterion. The blocker is specifically the two accepted, incorrect rewrites above.

### finding/s4-sol-r2-storeclausespan-doc-stale — non-blocking

File: [ast.py](/Users/kaygee/Code/loops/libs/lang/src/lang/ast.py:698), lines 698–705.

`StoreClauseSpan` still says its span covers the entire physical line and includes trailing comments that will be replaced. After `06844e55`, the intended behavior is the opposite: a sub-line clause span that excludes trailing comments.

This is fix-introduced truth drift from the F5 remediation.

